  "summary": "Carbon forms extensive chemistry because it is tetravalent and catenates strongly. Covalent bonding produces saturated and unsaturated hydrocarbons, while functional groups create families with predictable reactions. Homologous series and basic nomenclature organise the large subject. Combustion, oxidation, addition and substitution explain common transformations. Ethanol and ethanoic acid introduce oxidation, neutralisation and esterification, while soap chemistry explains micelles, hard water and detergents. The central lesson is that structure determines properties and reactions.",
